WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.272
A good questionnaire uses neutral, precise and single-purpose questions with suitable

00:00:05.272 --> 00:00:06.195
answer options.

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:11.889
Classify this survey question: “Which fruit do you like best?” The answer is clear

00:00:11.889 --> 00:00:16.744
and neutral. Which fruit do you like best? is classified as clear and neutral;

00:00:16.744 --> 00:00:19.172
surveys work best with precise neutral wording.

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:25.536
A student at a school fair asks “Do you agree that football is the only fun sport?”

00:00:25.536 --> 00:00:29.420
in a survey. What describes this question? Pause to choose and explain.

00:00:30.283 --> 00:00:35.827
A student at a school fair asks “Do you agree that football is the only fun sport?”

00:00:35.827 --> 00:00:40.718
in a survey. What describes this question? The answer is leading. Do you agree that

00:00:40.718 --> 00:00:45.284
football is the only fun sport? is classified as leading; surveys work best with

00:00:45.284 --> 00:00:46.262
precise neutral wording.
